					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-396696#post-1580670</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-396696/scp-872#post-1580670</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 04 Oct 2012 18:39:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Photosynthetic</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>361873</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>First off: this is a good SCP and you, Tanhony, should feel good. +1.</p> <p>I have a nitpick, though. You say that &quot;SCP-872 is composed of standard wood&quot;, but there is no such thing as &quot;standard wood&quot;. That's like saying &quot;a standard dog&quot;. May I change it to &quot;SCP-872 is composed of pine wood&quot;? Various pine woods are common and cheap in the sort of climate where it's implied this thing is from, and the change wouldn't really affect your phrasing otherwise.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
